      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: in-your-country-police-are-paid-to-protect-poor-liberals-and-rich-liberals-who-want-to-disarm-everybody; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a Black child’s face with a skeptical, 'I don’t believe you' expression to visually represent disbelief or mockery toward the claim that police are paid to protect 'poor liberals' and 'rich liberals who want to disarm everybody.' The image is juxtaposed with the text to imply that the statement is absurd or false. This meme is hateful because it targets Black people by using their image to convey a message that is racially coded and reinforces harmful stereotypes. The visual of a Black child is used to imply that the speaker is 'stupid' or 'uninformed' for believing such a thing, which is a form of racial stereotyping and dehumanization. The meme also promotes a false narrative about police and liberals, which is a form of propaganda. The overall intent is to provoke a reaction of disbelief or ridicule toward the political claim, while simultaneously using a Black person’s image to make the message more impactful and to imply that the target audience (liberals) is naive or foolish. The meme is harmful because it can contribute to racial prejudice and misunderstanding by associating Black people with ignorance or stupidity. The meme is also abusive because it uses a Black child’s image to mock and belittle the political views of liberals. The meme is misogynous because it implies that women are not capable of understanding complex political issues, which is a form of gender-based discrimination. The meme is propaganda because it is designed to influence opinions and actions toward a specific goal, which is to discredit the political views of liberals. The meme is harmful because it can contribute to racial prejudice and misunderstanding by associating Black people with ignorance or stupidity. The meme is also abusive because it uses a Black child’s image to mock and belittle the political views of liberals. The meme is misogynous because it implies that women are not capable of understanding complex political issues, which is a form of gender-based discrimination. The meme is propaganda because it is designed to influence opinions and actions toward a specific goal, which is to discredit the political views of liberals.",
