      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The skeptical child is mapped as the speaker of the political claim",
      "description": "The visual of the Black child with a skeptical expression is used to represent the speaker or believer of the text's claim — that police are paid to protect 'poor liberals' and 'rich liberals who want to disarm everybody.' The child's expression of disbelief is projected onto the text, implying that the speaker (the child) is mocking or ridiculing the claim, thereby mapping the child's persona onto the role of the political claimant. This is a form of analogical mapping where the visual entity (child) embodies the textual entity (the speaker of the claim).",
