      "label": "User projected onto the skeptical child's expression",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the Black child displaying a skeptical, 'I don’t believe you' expression. This projection is implicit, as the child's expression is used to represent the user's disbelief or mockery toward the political claim in the text. The child's direct gaze and hand-on-cheek gesture create a sense of personal address, making the user feel as if they are the one being mocked or ridiculed for believing the claim. This is a form of deictic projection where the user is implicitly mapped onto the child's persona as the speaker or believer of the claim.",
